## Delegations

| Agent / Tool | Owns | Spawn? | Reads |
|---|---|---|---|
| `@resume-writing` | All `.tex` edits | **Task** per pass | `context.md`, `reference/resume.md`, `persona.md` (lens), current `.tex`; **iter 1:** lens + pool; **iter >1:** defects JSON (+ persona only to interpret grader language) |
| `@resume-grading` | Defect enumeration (judgment only) | **Task** per pass | `reference/resume.md`, `reference/recruiting.md`, `persona.md` (lens), current `.tex` |
| `scripts/validate.py gates` | All deterministic artifact gates | orchestrator runs | the `.tex`, the `.pdf`, transient gate inputs; `--out` auto-derives beside `--inputs` under `.pipeline/` |
| `scripts/validate.py demerits` | Weighted demerits + display score + `loop_target_met` | orchestrator runs | grader-emitted defect JSON |
| `scripts/validate.py writer-loop` | Validate writer peak/continue decision | orchestrator runs | `writer_loop_status.json` + current `demerits.json` |
| `scripts/validate.py check-report` | Prose/JSON 1:1 enforcement on grader output | orchestrator runs | raw grader report text |
| `scripts/cleanup.py` | LaTeX + transient pipeline file removal | orchestrator runs | resume `.tex` path |

The orchestrator never duplicates an agent's work, never bypasses the validator, never lets the loop exit while a hard gate fails, and **never inlines writer/grader turns** — always Task spawn with the handoff contract above.

