## Step 2 — Resolve company.md  *(parallel with Step 4)*

**In:** `company_name`, `company_slug`, `applications_root`, Step 1 state object (comp, location, work model, `role_year`).

**Action:** Check `{applications_root}/{company_slug}/company.md`. If absent, create the folder and write from the template below. If present, read. `company.md` is write-once; never overwrite.

**Source priority when creating:**
1. **`reference/companies.md` row** (if present) — primary source for tier, interview funnel, bottleneck, acceptance estimate, and the Notes column (product/stack signal). Slice the row into Quick Facts and Interview Process; do not copy the table verbatim.
2. **The JD** — intern comp, locations, work model, clearance/eligibility, review windows, role-specific stack.
3. **Web search** — fill gaps when no row exists or Notes is thin (valuation, HQ, product description).

The prose block at the top expands the row's **Notes** (or web/JD research) into 2–4 readable sentences. Reference tone, not first person — this file is company intel for the pipeline, not a "why this company" essay. Step 1 reads this brief (especially Notes / Product focus / Stack) to set `differentiator`.

**Template (only when creating):**

```markdown
# {company_name}

{2-4 sentences: what the company builds, who it serves, and why it matters technically. Expand reference/companies.md Notes into prose; name the flagship product/platform if one exists. Specific, not marketing fluff.}

## Quick Facts

- **Tier:** {from reference/companies.md tier section, or "Unrated"}
- **HQ / offices:** {HQ + offices relevant to this application}
- **Valuation / signal:** {funding, market position, prestige markers — from Notes or web}
- **Product focus:** {core technical product/platform in one line}
- **Intern comp ({role_year} {track or role family}):** {from JD or null}
- **Work model:** {paid/unpaid, remote/hybrid/onsite, term length — from JD}
- **Clearance / eligibility:** {export-control, citizenship, class-year gates — from JD, or omit if none}

## Interview Process

| Stage | Format | Notes |
| ----- | ------ | ----- |
| Resume screen | {Human + ATS / referral-heavy / etc.} | {timing signal, e.g. review window} |
| OA | {platform or "None"} | {difficulty, style} |
| {additional stages from reference/companies.md Interview Process column} | {format} | {notes} |
| Behavioral | {if applicable} | {culture signal} |

**Estimated funnel:** {round count} · {LC/practical difficulty} · {OA platform} · {sys design?} · Bottleneck: {from reference/companies.md} · {acceptance estimate from reference/companies.md}

## Stack & Hiring Signal

- **Languages:** {from Notes, JD, and track — name what actually ships}
- **Domains:** {technical domains this company hires for}
- **What wins:** {what passes a resume screen here — grounded in reference/companies.md Notes and reference/recruiting.md, not generic advice}

## Sources

- {JD URL if available}
- `reference/companies.md` {tier section} row (interview format, bottleneck, acceptance estimate)
- {any web sources used for prose or facts}
```

**Constraint:** `company.md` is write-once. Never overwrite.

