## Orchestrator Constraints

- Never edit `.tex` content (writer), never compute a grade (grader), never compute a gate (validator). Run the validator; route its report. **Spawn** writer/grader via Task — never inline their work.
- Dispatch the writer in exactly two modes: **initial** (iter 1 / fresh rebalance) or **grading-response** (defects JSON primary). Never pass full grader prose to the writer — only `.pipeline/demerits.json` + mode tag.
- `persona.md` is a recruiter lens (bar, track, abstract screen criteria). Never put candidate entry names or include/omit tables in persona.
- Never grade or score an artifact whose hard gates fail.
- Loop exits only on `zero_demerits`, validated `writer_peak`, or `timeout` (10-iteration cap).
- Run Step 7 fit only when the loop ended with `hard_gates_pass`.
- Never let the grader compute demerit totals; `scripts/validate.py demerits` owns scoring and `loop_target_met`. The grader emits only the defect list.
- Run `scripts/validate.py writer-loop` after every grading-response write pass; re-dispatch the writer on failure or premature `peak` (step 9).
- Never persist standalone JSON grading artifacts — fold them into `grade.md` and run `scripts/cleanup.py clean --ship`.
- After ship, run `scripts/cleanup.py prune-root` from repo root to drop any stray pipeline JSON written outside `.pipeline/`.
- Run `scripts/cleanup.py clean --tex` after every `xelatex` compile during the loop and fit checks.
- Run all Python scripts via `.venv/bin/python` from repo root. If `.venv` is missing, create it (`python3 -m venv .venv`) and install `requirements.txt` before the pipeline.
- Always run `scripts/validate.py check-report` before scoring; re-dispatch the grader on failure.
- Keep `exempt_entries` honest and minimal — it is the one input that can soften the metric ceiling, and `scripts/validate.py` logs every exemption it applies.
- Never pass `context.md` to the grader. Never edit doctrine files, `template.tex`, or `template.cls`.
